# Real Pro DJ Link hardware captures may hold a DJ's library metadata —
# never committed. See HARDWARE-CAPTURE-PLAN.md and
# crates/prolink/tests/hardware_capture_replay.rs. `capture/` is where the
# capture tools write by default, `reference-*/` included: code and tests
# quote bytes from those sessions inline rather than reading them from
# here, so nothing breaks by their absence on another machine.
# `**/` because the directory the replay test actually reads is
# `crates/prolink/fixtures/hardware-capture/`, and a pattern with a slash in
# it anchors to this file's own directory — the un-prefixed form matched
# only a top-level `fixtures/` that has never existed, leaving real captures
# tracked.
**/fixtures/hardware-capture/
capture/
# A Wireshark capture of a booth network holds the same library metadata as
# the tools' own sessions, and the runbook asks for one every time.
*.pcapng
# Simulator track fixtures built from a capture (`sim-fixtures`): same real
# library metadata as the capture they come from, and rebuildable from it.
crates/decktective-core/fixtures/
